{%- comment -%}
  Catalogue filters — port of components/shop/catalogue-filters.tsx.

  Styled from the design system's Forms section: 11px camel field labels at
  0.18em, cream-filled controls with a sand rule, and pill chips — which the
  system reserves for badges and filter chips exactly like these.

  Every control is a LINK, not a form field. Each one is the current URL with one
  facet flipped, so filtering needs no JavaScript, no submit step and no client
  state: the URL is the state, it is shareable, and the back button undoes exactly
  one choice. In the React app lib/shopify/catalogue.ts built those hrefs; here
  Shopify builds them itself as `value.url_to_add` / `value.url_to_remove`. That
  swap is the whole reason this port deletes 241 lines.

  A link cannot be aria-pressed, so an applied filter carries aria-current
  instead — the fill is never the only thing saying it is on. Colourways carry
  their name as well as their swatch, for the same reason.

  Below `lg` the rail collapses into a <details>, closed to start with: expanded,
  it is around 450px of controls above the first product. <details> keeps that a
  disclosure the browser runs on its own, so the whole rail still works with
  JavaScript off, exactly as the links inside it do. What is NOT allowed to
  collapse with it is the fact that a filter is applied — so the summary carries
  the count of applied facets, and the panel is the same markup either way.

  TWO DELIBERATE DEVIATIONS, both forced by the platform and neither hidden:

  1. COUNTS ARE AGAINST THE FILTERED SET, not the whole catalogue. The React app
     computed facets from every product on purpose — "a count that changes as you
     narrow tells you nothing about what the filter would do". Shopify computes
     `value.count` against the current result set and exposes no whole-catalogue
     equivalent, so that rule cannot be kept here. It is a real regression, and
     it is written down rather than quietly accepted.

  2. THE "MADE TO ORDER" ROW IS GONE, and that is a fix. In the React app it was
     an availability row that counted zero, kept only because removing it meant
     touching QUERY_KEYS — the URL contract. Shopify has no such filter unless
     somebody creates one, so it simply does not appear, and a Still-open item
     closes itself.

  Filters are defined in Shopify's Search and Discovery app, not here. Until they
  are, `collection.filters` is empty and the rail says so instead of inventing
  facet values it cannot know.

  Accepts: collection, results_url
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign applied = 0
  for filter in collection.filters
    assign applied = applied | plus: filter.active_values.size
    if filter.type == 'price_range' and filter.min_value.value
      assign applied = applied | plus: 1
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{%- capture filter_panel -%}
  {%- if collection.filters.size == 0 -%}
    {% render 'alert', body: 'Catalogue filters are set up in Shopify, under the Search and Discovery app. Once category, size, colourway and availability are enabled there, this rail fills itself in.' %}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- for filter in collection.filters -%}
      {%- liquid
        assign group_classes = 'flex flex-col gap-3.5 border-t border-hairline pt-7'
        if forloop.first
          assign group_classes = 'flex flex-col gap-3.5'
        endif

        assign is_colour = false
        assign lowered = filter.label | downcase
        if lowered contains 'colour' or lowered contains 'color'
          assign is_colour = true
        endif

        assign is_size = false
        if lowered contains 'size'
          assign is_size = true
        endif
      -%}

      <section class="{{ group_classes }}">
        <h2 class="font-body text-micro uppercase tracking-label text-ink-subtle">{{ filter.label }}</h2>

        {%- if is_size -%}
          <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
            {%- for value in filter.values -%}
              <li>
                <a
                  href="{% if value.active %}{{ value.url_to_remove }}{% else %}{{ value.url_to_add }}{% endif %}"
                  {% if value.active %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
                  class="wl-tap inline-flex h-10 min-w-11 items-center justify-center rounded-xs border px-2 text-caption tracking-wide transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) {% if value.active %}border-brand bg-brand text-on-brand{% else %}border-line bg-canvas text-ink-body hover:border-brand hover:text-brand{% endif %}"
                >{{ value.label }}</a>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>

        {%- elsif is_colour -%}
          <ul class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
            {%- for value in filter.values -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                The swatch hex comes from the value's own swatch when Shopify has
                one; without it the chip falls back to a named pill, because a
                blank circle carries nothing at all.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <li>
                {%- if value.swatch.color -%}
                  <a
                    href="{% if value.active %}{{ value.url_to_remove }}{% else %}{{ value.url_to_add }}{% endif %}"
                    {% if value.active %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
                    title="{{ value.label }}"
                    style="background-color:{{ value.swatch.color }}"
                    class="wl-tap inline-block size-8 rounded-pill border border-line transition-shadow duration-(--duration-base) {% if value.active %}ring-2 ring-brand ring-offset-2{% else %}hover:ring-1 hover:ring-line{% endif %}"
                  ><span class="sr-only">{{ value.label }}</span></a>
                {%- else -%}
                  <a
                    href="{% if value.active %}{{ value.url_to_remove }}{% else %}{{ value.url_to_add }}{% endif %}"
                    {% if value.active %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
                    class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center rounded-pill border px-4 text-caption transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) {% if value.active %}border-brand bg-surface-muted text-ink{% else %}border-line bg-canvas text-ink-body hover:bg-surface-muted{% endif %}"
                  >{{ value.label }}</a>
                {%- endif -%}
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>

        {%- else -%}
          <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3.5">
            {%- for value in filter.values -%}
              <li>
                <a
                  href="{% if value.active %}{{ value.url_to_remove }}{% else %}{{ value.url_to_add }}{% endif %}"
                  {% if value.active %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}
                  class="flex min-h-11 items-center justify-between gap-4 text-small lg:min-h-8 transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) hover:text-brand {% if value.active %}text-brand{% else %}text-ink-body{% endif %}"
                >
                  <span>{{ value.label }}</span>
                  <span data-numeric class="text-caption text-on-inert">{{ value.count }}</span>
                </a>
              </li>
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}
      </section>
    {%- endfor -%}

    {%- if applied > 0 -%}
      <a
        href="{{ collection.url }}"
        class="inline-flex min-h-11 items-center self-start border-b border-line py-2 text-caption text-brand transition-colors duration-(--duration-base) hover:border-brand"
      >{{ 'catalogue.clear_all' | t }}</a>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endcapture -%}

<aside aria-label="{{ 'catalogue.filters' | t }}" class="lg:sticky lg:top-[calc(var(--header-height)+1rem)]">
  <details class="group border-b border-rule pb-6 lg:hidden">
    <summary class="flex min-h-11 cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-micro uppercase tracking-label text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
      <span>
        {{ 'catalogue.filters' | t }}
        {%- if applied > 0 -%}
          <span data-numeric class="text-ink-subtle"> ({{ applied }})</span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </span>
      {% render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-right', class: 'size-4 rotate-90 text-ink-subtle transition-transform duration-(--duration-base) group-open:-rotate-90' %}
    </summary>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-block pt-7">{{ filter_panel }}</div>
  </details>

  <div class="hidden lg:flex lg:flex-col lg:gap-block">{{ filter_panel }}</div>
</aside>
